  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 60af0432a3c869e48a591344a8dafd71, type: 3}
  m_Name: ClinPhys 3
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  question: 'Your research team is planning a Phase III clinical trial. In addition
    to measuring tumor size changes, you suggest adding patient-reported quality-of-life
    measures and overall survival as additional outcomes.


    <b>Why would a physician
    recommend these additional endpoints?</b>'
  explanation: "Physicians bring a real-world clinical perspective to trial design,
    helping make sure the outcomes being measured\u2014called endpoints\u2014truly
    matter for patients. While changes like tumor shrinkage are important signs that
    a treatment is working, physicians also emphasize measuring things like quality
    of life, symptom relief, and survival, which show how a new therapy affects patients\u2019
    daily lives and overall health beyond the lab."
  correctAnswer: To make sure the trial focuses on outcomes that are clinically meaningful
    for patients
  incorrectAnswer1: To make the study more statistically significant by collecting
    more data
  incorrectAnswer2: To meet the required rules and guidelines for running a clinical
    trial
  incorrectAnswer3: "To improve the chances of FDA approval even if the treatment
    isn\u2019t effective"
  questionRole: Physician
  questionType: MultipleChoice
  questionStage: Clinical
